a)   That City of Langford Council consider a partnership with the West Side municipalities to
             continue with an independent analysis of a Sewage Treatment facility for educated decision
             making;
        b) The budget for this work could be considered in the 2016 budget approval process;
        c)   That the City of Langford investigate the legalities of proceeding within the CRD framework;
             and,
        d)   That the Sewage Oversight Committee be permitted to make presentations and discuss
             partnerships and processes with the other West Side Councils and Staff, to the benefit of the
             City of Langford.

That Council:
        1. Proceed with the consideration of this Temporary Use Permit for a school on the property at
            #115 -963 Langford Parkway for a period of three (3) years;
        2. Direct staff to amend the Zoning Bylaw to allow for a school in the CD2 —Area A (Hull's Field)
            zone;

That Council approve 2016 funding for the following applications:
       a) Your Literacy Connection - $500 and use of the trolley for the Learning Tour;
       b) Metchosin Farmers' Institute —cost of tent rental for Luxton Fall Fair (approx.. $350);
       c) Royal Canadian Legion - $2,000 for Remembrance Day luncheon;
       d) Fort Rodd Hill and Fisgard Lighthouse - $1,000 for Canada Day celebration;
       e) Vancouver Island South Film and Media Commission - $2,000 to promote the industry;
       f) Goldstream Nature House and HAT - $1,000 for the Chums educational program;
       g) Belmont and Royal Bay schools - $5,000 each for combined dry grad;
       h) Greater Victoria Bike to Work Society -$1,500 for Bike to Work Week;
       i) YMCA-YWCA of Greater Victoria — use of the trolley for event October 20, 2016; and
       j) Victoria Real Estate Board — use of trolley for tour to promote Langford.

That Council:

     1.   Direct staff to apply to the Community Emergency Preparedness Fund, Structural Flood
          Mitigation program for the Irwin Dam Improvements;


          AND

     2.   Direct staff to retain a geotechnical engineer to design and cost the Irwin Dam improvements
          funded from the City's Infrastructure Replacement Fund;

That Council approve the following for the Thunder Bowl Football Event taking place August
      26th, 2016 at City Centre Park:
      1. Waive the fee for Westhills turf rental;
      2. Waive the fee for Westhills Stadium rental;
      3. Vacant stadium suite fee waived; and
      4. Revenue from the Big Screen advertising.

That Council adopt the following resolution:

Whereas the British Columbia Speculation Tax imposes an unfair tax burden on British Columbians and
other Canadians who wish to purchase or own a second home in British Columbia, and;

Whereas the tax was imposed on municipalities without consultation or economic modelling of its
impact, and;

Whereas the Government of British Columbia has already removed Parksville, the Gulf Islands, the Juan
de Fuca Electoral Area and other areas due to pressure from various Members of the BC Legislature and;

Therefore be it resolved that the City of Langford calls upon the BC Government to allow municipalities
to opt out of this new housing speculation tax and;

Be it further resolved that the City of Langford calls upon the BC Government to put any funds received
from a speculation tax on housing towards an affordable housing fund and;

Be it further resolved that the City of Langford put the resolution for debate and consideration at the
2018 UBCM Convention in conjunction with a covering letter from the Mayor.

That Council award the construction of the West Shore Parkway Sewer Lift Station to the lowest compliant
bidder, so long as the bid is within budget, and fund the project from the New Building Canada
Infrastructure grant for the West Shore Parkway Completion project;
